{
  "case_id": "2017-16-476",
  "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Olson, isn't that what the government does whenever it preempts state laws? It says you can't regulate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Theodore B. Olson",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the consequence of that is that the -- the states could regulate according to the standards established by the federal government with respect to the regulation of interstate commerce, and if the states chose not to do that, the field was left to the federal government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry. Does the injunction tell the governor that he has to enforce this law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLSON: No, it doesn't. What the -- what -- the governor's responsibility to enforce the law -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: There is nothing here telling this state that it has to enforce this law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What's the difference between that and this law is unconstitutional? This law is preempted or just a simple ruling by the court, this law is preempted? Period, end of story."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: And I'm curious, why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: This partial repeal is forbidden."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question is, if we're asking the severability question the Chief Justice posed to you, one of the questions we have is what Congress would have done in -- in a different world? Now, that's a very hard question to answer, but that's the question we were posed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would Congress have wanted to have the first four prohibitions in (1) and the prohibitions in (2), if it couldn't have the \"licensed or authorized by law\" provision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When we first filed our TRO, we went against the state and we went against the private parties. We got a TRO against both, and then there was an unclean hands argument that arose only with the private parties, so the district court enjoined only the -- the states."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Give me a one-sentence answer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think Mr. Olson has boiled down the state's case to what I take to be his two basic arguments. This is a commandeering problem, he says, because New Jersey is forced to keep a law on its books and there's no accompanying comprehensive federal regime. Both of those arguments are incorrect."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0002-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you're trying to figure out what constitutes an authorization to operate a sports gambling scheme, any law that says everybody can't do it, except for you two or three, that's an authorization."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Have I got that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. WALL",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that is their argument, but I think it doesn't make sense for the simple reason Mr. Clement gave."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I've got your argument right just now, just say yes. Otherwise forget it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's your selective -- your selective prosecution theory, that they're permitting fantasy teams?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are four states that are -- are permitted to continue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.91,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So why don't we -\u00ad why don't we legalize -- this is a hypothetical -- marijuana because all of -- and all drugs, because there's a rampant market out there for those drugs, but we've made a policy choice that we don't want the state involved in promoting that type of enterprise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is this any different?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2017-16-476",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "080dd34af2dc283bd74eccb81ed89f783825240d14af3a45f6e8c2eefe8a3062",
      "evidence_id": "ev-080dd34af2dc-0003-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
